      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This case report presents a 68-year-old woman with a symptomatic coronary artery fistula. Usually these rare congenital malformations are symptom-free but in this patient the fistula began to cause various arrhythmias after it thrombosed. Her symptoms resolved completely after connective surgery."},
